`@startuml f1-operator-creates-secret
title F1 — Operator creates a secret

|Operator|
start
:Open Secrets page in UI;

|UI|
:Render form (name, value, scope);

|Operator|
:Fill form, click Save;

|UI|
:POST /secrets
 (bearer_token, name, value, scope)
 to API Gateway;
:Show "saving..." indicator;

|API Gateway|
:Validate bearer_token;
:Route to Secret Service
 POST /secrets { name, value, scope };
note right
  GW's only logic.
  Auth + route.
  No validation,
  no business,
  no writes of its own.
end note

|Secret Service|
:Validate input shape;
:Validate scope (user or project);
:Encrypt value (KMS-backed data key);
:Persist ciphertext + metadata;
:Write audit log entry
 (operator_id, action=create);
:Return 201 { secret_id };

|API Gateway|
:Return 201 { secret_id } to UI;

|UI|
:Hide indicator;
:Display "secret saved" toast;

|Operator|
:See confirmation;

stop

note right
  Write-only path: UI -> GW (auth) -> SS.
  GW has no business logic, just auth and route.
  All writes happen in SS.
end note

@enduml